[gd_scene load_steps=14 format=3 uid="uid://b3slasharc0001"]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/slash_arc.gd" id="1_script"]

; ── Magical energy-sword cut — iter 73 phasing rework ────────────────────
; Iter 29 baseline: three Line2D layers (OuterHalo/Halo/Core) + two
; particle bursts. Iter 73 adds:
;   • HiltFlash node — bright cyan-white anticipation pulse at the
;     swing origin. Tells the eye "the hero just swung" in the first
;     0.08s, before the arc's sweep registers.
;   • GhostArc — fourth widest, low-alpha Line2D that lags 0.06s
;     behind the main arc to read as motion-blur trailing the cut.
;
; The shoot has anticipation/travel/connection/theme phases the eye
; reads. The slash now matches by adding anticipation (HiltFlash) +
; motion blur (GhostArc), keeping peak (the three arcs) and lingering
; longer (DURATION 0.25 → 0.32 in slash_arc.gd).
;
; Layer order (back to front):
;   GhostArc    — widest, lowest-alpha cyan-magenta trail (motion blur)
;   OuterHalo   — wide, purple-magenta atmospheric glow
;   Halo        — mid, gold-magenta-cyan gradient
;   Core        — narrow bright cream-white edge
;   HiltSparkle — particle burst at origin (wizard's hand)
;   TipBurst    — particle burst at arc peak (blade tip)
;   HiltFlash   — bright Polygon2D anticipation pulse at origin
;                  (drawn last = topmost for the brief flash window)

; Width curves
